// The French app's sheets for the verb track (verb-track.js with
// verb-track-fr.js): the same shape as the German ones — the structure
// as coloured blocks, one line on why, up to four rules, a table or a
// list, examples, the trap — and a quiz that asks about every point.
// Written for a Spanish speaker: the explanations lean on what Spanish
// already does (copretérito ≈ imparfait, subjuntivo ≈ subjonctif) and
// warn where it misleads (j'ai 20 ans, je suis allé, si j'avais).
//
// Markup: **bold** · [[verb]] in the tense's colour · {{è}} a changed
// letter · ~~struck~~ · *italic*.
//
//   quiz  { at, k: "type" | "pick" | "odd" | "order" | "why", q, a, o?,
//         why, chk? } — chk [inf, form kind, person]: the engine must
//         give the same answer (tools/verb-track/test-content-fr.mjs)
//         { at, g: "form" | "aux", t: form kind, p, v: verb set
//         (verb-track-fr.js VXF_GQ_SETS), fb: fallback verbs, ask?, lbl? }
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────

